 "briefing": "# Zepto Pre-Meeting Briefing: 17 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified changes at Zepto for 16 October to 15 November 2026 could be confirmed. Every search query returned an error (\"No valid search results found\") and no source pages were retrieved. The briefing therefore contains no sourced facts, and no item below can be dated within the window. The gaps are listed below so the research can be completed before the meeting.\n\n## What Changed: Four Categories\n\n### News\nNo verified news items. No regulatory, legal, city-expansion, operational, leadership-commentary, or financial-result items were retrieved.\n\n### Product and Service Launches\nNo verified launches. No app features, category or delivery offerings, new cities or dark stores, subscription or pricing programs, or new brands were retrieved.\n\n### Executive and Other Hires\nNo verified hires or departures. No CEO, CFO, CTO, COO, CPO, VP-level, or board changes were retrieved.\n\n### Deals\nNo verified deals. No funding rounds, secondary sales, IPO filings, acquisitions, partnerships, or investments were retrieved.\n\n## Steps to Complete Before 17 November\n\n1. **Check primary sources first:** Zepto's official website, newsroom, blog, and LinkedIn page, filtered to 16 October to 15 November 2026.\n2. **Check regulatory filings:** Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA21) filings for board and capital changes, and BSE and NSE announcements if any listing-related disclosures exist.\n3. **Check business news outlets:** Entrackr, Inc42, and Economic Times, using each site's own search for Zepto with date filters.\n4. **Re-run the search:** Once the search service works, run the research again. Any item without a URL and a date inside the window should be dropped or flagged as \"date not verified.\"\n\n## Provisional Open Questions for the Meeting\n\nThese questions are general to Zepto's business and are not yet grounded in changes from the research window. Replace or refine them once the checks above are complete.\n\n1. What are Zepto's current priorities for dark-store expansion and unit economics, and how have these shifted recently?\n2. Which product or service changes have you launched or are planning, and how are they performing against your targets?\n3. Have there been any changes in senior leadership or capital-raising plans that affect our planned partnership or engagement?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Zepto official website (primary source to check for news, launches, and leadership): https://www.zeptonow.com\n[2] Ministry of Corporate Affairs, MCA21 portal (regulatory filings to check): https://www.mca.gov.in\n[3] Entrackr (business news to check): https://entrackr.com\n[4] Inc42 (business news to check): https://inc42.com\n[5] Economic Times (business news to check): https://economictimes.indiatimes.com\n\n*Note: Sources 1 to 5 are the places to verify, not sources for any fact in this briefing. No fact in this briefing has been verified against them.*",
